  "about": "The map: the fractals you can choose, and for each one the stages of its journey. The page reads its text, labels, sources, framing and colours from here. Escape-time stages: re and im are the centre of the view, span its height in the complex plane, turn its rotation in degrees, iter the iteration limit at the bottom of the dive; a Julia stage adds its constant k (kre, kim). Where a stage has a period, its centre is the nucleus of a copy with that period, and tests/stages.test.mjs checks it. Mandelbulb stages: power, camera distance from the centre, yaw and pitch in degrees, field of view. Buddhabrot stages: the view, and the iteration limits for the red, green and blue counts. Colours (palette, flow, density, glow), routes and sounds are artistic choices.",
